    "result": "Perfect! All tests are now passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n### 1. Missing Export in Governance Module (governance.test.js)\n**Problem**: The test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from `./index.js`, but it was only available in the default export.\n\n**Solution**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` at the top of the index.js file.\n\n### 2. Toxicity Metric Signature Mismatch (eval/index.test.js)\n**Problem**: The `toxicityMetric` function was defined as `(outputs, bannedTerms)` but `runEvaluations` calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`. This caused the references array to be treated as banned terms, flagging all outputs as toxic.\n\n**Solution**: Changed the signature to `(outputs, references, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` so it accepts the references parameter (even though it's not used for toxicity checking) and defaults to the standard banned terms. Added a JSDoc block as requested.\n\n**Test Results**: \u2705 All 28 tests passing across 8 test files.",
